// The variables the process a program runs in was started with.
//
// `docs/specs/io.md` states what a read gives back. It is one `extern` declaration away from a
// JVM method, which `docs/specs/interop.md` states, and a variable nothing set is `None` rather
// than a failure, because a process that was started without one is an ordinary case.
/// The variable called `name`, and `None` where the process was started without it.
extern static read(name: String) -> Option<String> = "java.lang.System.getenv"
